      "content": "Conventions of this environment:\n- To use a tool, make a real tool call with complete arguments, every time.\n- Your earlier tool calls may be shown with their arguments replaced by {ref, name, want}. These are records the system writes after the fact. Never write one yourself: it runs nothing.\n- When a tool's output may be long, state in `want` what you are looking for. A result that starts with a tag like [os:1k2j3h 305L keywords 1/1] was reduced to that; the rest is available from output_read with the handle.\n- An earlier reply of yours may appear as a condensed record: a line like [os:1k2j3h troubleshot] (handle, then what that turn did) followed by the lines that were kept. entry_read opens its gotchas, steps, transcript or summary. Open one only for a specific reason the kept lines cannot meet.\n- Start a line with ! if it must survive when this conversation is condensed, !! if it is critical. Unmarked lines may be dropped.\n- When the person asks to see something, copy it, save it as a file, run a command or apply a config, put that content in a handoff block: a code fence whose info string is handoff:copy, handoff:file <name>, handoff:command, handoff:view <html|json|csv> or handoff:config, followed by a short title. Code that only explains stays in plain fences."
